"<a>Optics</a>",
"Units follow the lectures, one per set of lecture notes, then the rest of the course in the order of the syllabus. Each card lists the Physics II worksheets. A demo can appear in more than one lecture: it has one card, in the first lecture that uses it, and later lectures link to it. Section numbers are volume:section in OpenStax University Physics, and sections with no activity yet are listed under each unit. Every demo here is also on the <a>Physics II</a> page, by topic. Looking for one subject? Every demo is also under <a>All demos by topic</a>.",
"Lecture {#} · Electric charge",
"The four forces and the elementary charge, conductors, insulators and semiconductors, charging by contact and by induction, conservation of charge, and Coulomb’s law with superposition of the forces from several charges.",
"Also used in this unit: <a>Coulomb Sandbox</a> <span>(card under <a>Lecture {#} · Electric fields</a>; {#}:{#})</span>",
"Lecture {#} · Electric fields",
"The field as force per charge, F = qE beside F = mg, finding a charge from a measured field, superposition of fields, and the charge densities λ, σ and ρ.",
"Lecture {#} · Dipoles",
"The dipole field on its axis with the binomial approximation, the dipole moment p = qd, the torque p × E, and the work and potential energy of a dipole in a field.",
"Lecture {#} · Fields of charge distributions",
"Integrating over a line, an arc and a ring of charge, then two charged disks, which lead to the parallel plate capacitor.",
"Also used in this unit: <a>Coulomb Sandbox</a> <span>(card under <a>Lecture {#} · Electric fields</a>; {#}:{#}, {#}:{#})</span>",
"Lecture {#} · Flux and Gauss’s law",
"Flux through flat, curved and closed surfaces, and why the flux of a point charge through any closed surface is Q/ε₀.",
"Lecture {#} · Gauss’s law examples",
"A long line of charge, a charged conducting wire inside and out, a conducting sphere, and the field inside a hollow conductor.",
"Also used in this unit: <a>Gauss's Law</a> with <a>Worksheet: Gauss's Law</a> <span>(card under <a>Lecture {#} · Flux and Gauss’s law</a>; {#}:{#}, {#}:{#})</span> · <a>Charging by Induction</a> <span>(card under <a>Lecture {#} · Electric charge</a>; {#}:{#})</span>",
"Lecture {#} · Voltage and potential",
"Potential energy kQq/r, potential as a height above a reference point, and energy conservation for a charge accelerated through a potential difference.",
"Also used in this unit: <a>Coulomb Sandbox</a> with <a>Worksheet: Electric Field and Potential</a> <span>(card under <a>Lecture {#} · Electric fields</a>; {#}:{#}, {#}:{#})</span>",
"Lecture {#} · Potential of charge distributions",
"Adding the potentials of point charges, then the potential of a line of charge and of a ring.",
"Lecture {#} · The gradient operator",
"Line integrals and conservative forces, ΔV as the line integral of −E, and E = −∇V in Cartesian, cylindrical and spherical coordinates, with equipotentials and conductors.",
"Lecture {#} · Capacitors and capacitance",
"Q = CV and C = ε₀A/d, the energy ½CV² and the energy density ½ε₀E², dielectrics and κ, and dielectric strength and breakdown.",
"Also used in this unit: <a>Charging by Induction</a> <span>(card under <a>Lecture {#} · Electric charge</a>; {#}:{#})</span>",
"Lecture {#} · Capacitor circuits",
"<span>Vol {#} · Ch. {#}, {#}</span><span>{#} of {#} sections with an activity</span>",
"Current as the rate of flow of charge, Kirchhoff’s rules, and capacitors in series, in parallel and in combination.",
"<span>{#}:{#}</span> Electromotive Force",
"<span>{#}:{#}</span> Kirchhoff's Rules",
"Also used in this unit: <a>Capacitors and Dielectrics</a> <span>(card under <a>Lecture {#} · Capacitors and capacitance</a>; {#}:{#})</span>",
"Lecture {#} · Resistors and resistivity",
"Conventional current and the current density J = σE, Ohm’s law and R = ρL/A, how resistance changes with temperature, drift velocity in copper, power, and resistors in series and parallel.",
"Also used in this unit: <a>Circuits</a> with <a>Worksheet: Kirchhoff's Rules</a> <span>(card under <a>Lecture {#} · Capacitor circuits</a>; {#}:{#}, {#}:{#}, {#}:{#}, {#}:{#}, {#}:{#})</span>",
"Lecture {#} · RC circuits",
"The loop equation as a differential equation, Q(t) = Q_max({#} − e^(−t/RC)), and the time constant RC, when a capacitor reaches {#} % of its charge.",
"Also used in this unit: <a>Circuits</a> with <a>Worksheet: RC Time Constant</a> <span>(card under <a>Lecture {#} · Capacitor circuits</a>; {#}:{#})</span>",
"Lecture {#} · Magnets, part {#}",
"Magnetic field lines beside electric ones, the force qv × B, teslas and gauss, and the circular and helical motion of a charge in a uniform field.",
"Magnets, part {#}: forces on currents and the Hall effect",
"The rest of the course, in the order of the syllabus. The force on a wire, the torque on a current loop and its dipole moment, the Hall effect, and the applications of magnetic forces.",
"Also used in this unit: <a>Magnetic Fields of Currents</a> <span>(card under <a>Lecture {#} · Magnets, part {#}</a>; {#}:{#}, {#}:{#})</span> · <a>Charges in Magnetic Fields</a> <span>(card under <a>Lecture {#} · Magnets, part {#}</a>; {#}:{#}, {#}:{#})</span>",
"Also used in this unit: <a>Magnetic Fields of Currents</a> with <a>Worksheet: Fields and Forces of Straight Wires</a> with <a>Worksheet: Fields of Loops and Solenoids</a> <span>(card under <a>Lecture {#} · Magnets, part {#}</a>; {#}:{#}, {#}:{#}, {#}:{#}, {#}:{#}, {#}:{#}, {#}:{#})</span>",
"Also used in this unit: <a>Circuits</a> with <a>Worksheet: RLC Oscillations</a> <span>(card under <a>Lecture {#} · Capacitor circuits</a>; {#}:{#}, {#}:{#}, {#}:{#}, {#}:{#}, {#}:{#})</span>",
"Also used in this unit: <a>Circuits</a> with <a>Worksheet: AC Resonance</a> with <a>Worksheet: Reactance and Phase</a> with <a>Worksheet: Power in an AC Circuit</a> <span>(card under <a>Lecture {#} · Capacitor circuits</a>; {#}:{#}, {#}:{#}, {#}:{#}, {#}:{#}, {#}:{#})</span> · <a>Transformers</a> <span>(card under <a>Induction and inductance</a>; {#}:{#})</span>",
